  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NL contribution to the State and Peacebuilding Fund 2.0  - a multi-donor trust fund from the World Bank Group to enhance its work in FCV-settings.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPF is a WB multi-donor trust fund, aimed at assisting the implementation of the WB Fragility, Conflict &amp; Violence (FCV) Strategy at country, regional, and global levels, driving innovation and engaging all world regions, global themes, and Global Practices (GPs). In line with the WB&#x2019;s increased focus on greater flexibility, SPF is a vehicle for the quick mobilization of finance. The Development Objective of the SPF is to enhance and expand the frontiers of World Bank engagement in addressing the drivers and impacts of FCV and strengthening the resilience of countries and affected populations, communities and institutions. SPF is a small demand based fund, mainly providing funding for internal Bank projects aimed at enhancing the Bank&apos;s functioning in FCV settings. SPF also provides small Recipient-Executed (RE) grants with public or civil society partners to strengthen local capacity. SPF has global reach: it supports IDA countries but also non-member and middle income countries.</narrative>
  </description>
